          "skill": "inferences",
          "passage": "Aerospace engineer Aprille Ericsson, who designs and analyzes the dynamics of spacecraft instruments at NASA Goddard Space Flight Center, has noted two facts about how large orbiting observatories actually behave. First, the pointing accuracy demanded of such instruments is set at very fine angular tolerances, so that even subtle disturbances on board the spacecraft can carry the line of sight off target. Second, the moving components mounted on the spacecraft, including reaction wheels and articulating mechanisms, do not act on a perfectly rigid body; their motion couples instead with the bending and twisting of the spacecraft's flexible structure. Taken together, these observations imply that, when engineers try to predict the in-orbit pointing performance of a large instrument, ______",
