          "passage": "In his 1841 essay Self-Reliance, Ralph Waldo Emerson set out to defend the authority of individual intuition against the pressures of imitation and consensus. The age, in his view, had grown over-attached to received opinion: men measured their own thoughts by the assent of their neighbors and dismissed any flash of insight that the world had not already approved. Emerson sought to overturn that habit and to install a different standard of intellectual courage in its place. *He argues that genuine intellectual achievement requires acting on one's own perception even when conventional opinion runs strongly the other way, and that the thinker who defers to the verdict of the multitude forfeits the very faculty by which truth is reached.*",
