          "passage": "Soil microbial ecologist Wei Cheng, working at the University of California, Santa Cruz, uses isotope-labeling experiments to trace how living plant roots reshape soil microbial activity. In his 2009 paper introducing the rhizosphere priming effect, Cheng showed that roots can stimulate microbes to decompose previously stable organic matter, accelerating carbon and nitrogen cycling beyond what bare-soil studies predict. Researchers ______ build on this work argue that omitting living roots from soil-carbon models leads to systematic underestimates of decomposition rates.",
